## Summary

Bounded non-GPU SM-505 release-gate reconciliation for #50.

- preserves the accepted SM-501 GTX 1650 SUPER timing result and documents its source-identity boundary;
- records the retained renderer-owned memory estimate;
- identifies the release-blocking normal-game presentation gap: WebGPU can initialize, but the live RenderScene bridge still presents through WebGL2;
- records stale PWA/deployment cache identity (runtime r26 vs documented r1);
- enumerates the exact target-hardware evidence required after a real normal-game WebGPU presentation candidate exists;
- updates the execution ledger/index.

## Deliberate non-actions

- leaves #50 open;
- does **not** set `AUTO_WEBGPU_ENABLED=true`;
- does **not** run or request any new physical-GPU validation;
- does **not** start #37 / SM-602;
- does **not** revise SM-501 acceptance or pull later fidelity work into the release gate.

## Verification

Current pre-promotion main has all five hosted checks green, including clean package/extraction and WebGL2/WebGPU browser validation. This PR is documentation-only; required hosted checks should still pass unchanged.

Refs #50.
